# --- Supabase --------------------------------------------------------------
# Same project the tracker (../schema.sql) writes to.
# Project Settings -> API. Use the *service_role* key — server-side only,
# never exposed to the browser.
SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...service_role...

# --- Auth ------------------------------------------------------------------
# BOTH of these are required. If either is missing the dashboard fails closed:
# src/proxy.ts serves 503 on every route rather than exposing the data.
#
# The single shared password for the whole dashboard. Compared in constant time
# against what the login form submits (src/lib/auth/session.ts).
DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=choose-a-long-random-password

# HMAC key that signs the session cookie. Anyone who knows this can mint a valid
# session, so treat it exactly like the service-role key. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Changing it invalidates every existing session (i.e. logs everyone out).
SESSION_SECRET=64-hex-chars-from-openssl-rand-hex-32

# --- Fee model ---------------------------------------------------------
# MUST mirror whatever the tracker is actually running with (its config.py /
# .env.local), not just these defaults — if the two drift, every net-margin
# figure and every "live deal" in this dashboard will be wrong. See the header
# comment in src/lib/constants.ts. Check the tracker's live .env.local before
# deploying.
SELLER_FEE=0
BUYER_FEE=0.075
BUYER_FIXED=0.69
SHIPPING_IN=4.50

# Required margin: whichever of the flat floor and the percentage demands more.
# config.py's MARGIN_RATE default is 0.18; the crossover is
# TARGET_MARGIN / MARGIN_RATE, i.e. ~278 EUR at these values.
TARGET_MARGIN=50
MARGIN_RATE=0.18

# Extra margin demanded while a model is still on its hand-written seed price
# (model_prices.is_seed), before real comps replace it.
SEED_MARGIN_MULTIPLIER=1.6

# The deal gate tests the *haggled* offer, price * (1 - OFFER_DISCOUNT), not the
# raw asking price — matching pricing.evaluate. Getting this wrong makes the
# dashboard's deal list disagree with the alert feed.
OFFER_DISCOUNT=0.20

# Floor on how far below the reference a listing may sit, as a fraction of it.
# RE-ENABLED at 0.65 (2026-08-26) — stricter than it has ever been. MUST match
# the tracker; config.py is also 0.65. A listing must ask at least 65% of what
# the model is worth or it is rejected before any margin maths. This is a
# load-bearing filter: expect a much shorter deal list, and expect it to miss
# some real bargains along with the fakes. Set to 0 to disable.
MIN_PLAUSIBLE_RATIO=0.65

# Sanity band — outside this a price is a typo, a bundle or a scam.
MIN_SANE_PRICE=50
MAX_SANE_PRICE=1000

# Scope cap for listings with NO reference price behind them — the tracker's
# bootstrap path. Mirrors config.py's MAX_ALERT_PRICE.
MAX_DEAL_PRICE=450

# Scope cap for listings that DO have a reference price, which is every listing
# in this dashboard's deal list. Mirrors config.py's MAX_CAPITAL_PRICE. Once a
# model has a reference the margin gate is a real test, so this only bounds
# capital at risk on one purchase and sits much higher. Set it to 350 and the
# dashboard hides the high-end deals the tracker exists to find.
MAX_CAPITAL_PRICE=500

# Comps needed before a model's price stops being called low-confidence.
# Mirrors config.py's MIN_COMPS.
MIN_COMPS=5

# --- Alert scope -----------------------------------------------------------
# These are NOT part of the margin maths. They are the scope rejections
# alert_loop applies before a listing is ever evaluated, and the dashboard has
# to apply them too or its deal list is wider than the alert feed. See the
# second section of src/lib/constants.ts.

# Product families that may appear as a deal. Mirrors
# alert_loop.ALERTING_FAMILIES. iPhones are in the tracker's registry so it can
# learn what they resell for — data without alerts — so 'phone' is deliberately
# absent. Adding it here would put handsets in the deal list that the bot will
# never send.
ALERTING_FAMILIES=gpu

# Bottom condition tier, excluded. Mirrors config.py's BLOCKED_CONDITIONS.
# 'fair' deliberately stays: a cosmetic flaw on a working card is the discount a
# flip is built on.
BLOCKED_CONDITIONS=has_given_it_all

# Comma-separated seller ids to hide. Mirrors config.py's BLOCKED_SELLERS, and
# must be kept in step with it — a seller worth blocking from the alert feed is
# one worth hiding from the deal list. Empty by default.
BLOCKED_SELLERS=
